Let nums be a list of -1, 2, 1, and -4.
Let target be 1.
Sort nums.
Let n be count of nums.
Let best start at 0.
Let best distance start at 2147483647.

For every i from 0 to n - 1:
    Let lo start at i + 1.
    Let hi be n - 1.
    Repeat while lo < hi:
        Let total be item i of nums + item lo of nums + item hi of nums.
        Let difference be total - target.
        If difference < 0:
            Set difference to 0 - difference.
        If difference < best distance:
            Set best distance to difference.
            Set best to total.
        If total < target:
            Add 1 to lo.
        Otherwise:
            Subtract 1 from hi.

Print best.
